uired of Buyer pursuant to Rule 3-14 of Securities and Exchange Commission =
Regulation S-X (the
=93Audit=94), of the income statements of the Property for the last complet=
e fiscal year immediately preceding the Closing Date and the stub period th=
rough the Closing Date (the =93Audit Period=94). Seller shall reasonably co=
operate (at
no cost or liability of any kind to Seller) with Buyer=92s auditor in the c=
onduct of the Audit. Without limiting the foregoing, (a)&nbsp;Buyer or its =
designated independent or other auditor may audit the operating statements =
of the Property, at
Buyer=92s expense and, upon Buyer=92s reasonable prior written request, Sel=
ler shall allow Buyer=92s auditors reasonable access to such books and reco=
rds maintained by Seller in respect to the Property and pertaining to the A=
udit Period as
necessary to conduct the Audit; and (b)&nbsp;Seller shall use reasonable ef=
forts to provide to Buyer such existing financial information as may be rea=
sonably required by Buyer and required for Buyer=92s auditors to conduct th=
e Audit, provided,
however, that the ongoing obligations of Seller shall be limited to providi=
ng such information or documentation as may be in the possession or control=
 of Seller, the Seller=92s accountants or the applicable property or asset =
manager, at no cost
or liability of any kind to any of such parties, and in the format the Sell=
er has maintained such information. </font></p> <p style=3D"margin-top:12px=
